, 248.92, 132.54], ["intra-pair match 0.15 mm. CEC / HPD / DDC connect directly (CM5 has", 248.92, 134.59], ["internal pull-up / pull-down, 5 V tolerant). No ESD parts on CM5.", 248.92, 136.63], ["J3 pin 18 (+5V to sink) from +5V rail via F1 500 mA polyfuse.", 248.92, 138.68], ["Pin 14 UTILITY not used. Shields / DDC GND -> DGND.", 248.92, 140.72], ["PWR_FLAGs: these rails are supplied by the PC104 bus (EPS board).", 220.98, 234.14], ["CM5 5 V in: pins 77-87, up to 2.5 A, from +5V; C2/C3 = bulk", 220.98, 236.19], ["decoupling near the module. GPIO_VREF (78) -> CM5_3.3V, so", 220.98, 238.23], ["GPIO0-27 are 3.3 V logic. CM5_3.3V (84/86, 600 mA max)", 220.98, 240.28], ["also feeds the Ethernet LEDs and the camera (J4 pin 22).", 220.98, 242.32], ["Raspberry Pi CM5", 384.81, 52.46], ["PC104 connectors", 51.82, 32.5], ["Ethernet (CM5 side): Pair0..3 -> U3 TRD0..3", 444.5, 55.85], ["nLED3 (activity, green) -> ETH_LEDG", 444.5, 57.89], ["nLED2 (speed, yellow) -> ETH_LEDY", 444.5, 59.94], ["All CM5 GND pins -> DGND (= PC104 DGND)", 444.5, 61.98], ["HDMI0", 248.92, 42.3], ["Unused CM5 pins are marked no-connect. USB 2.0 (103/105) goes to the USB-C block on sheet 2.", 384.81, 328.4], ["nRPIBOOT (93) is NC -> for rpiboot eMMC programming pull it low with a jumper, or program on a CM5 IO board.", 384.81, 330.45], ["VBAT (76) NC -> no RTC backup. WL/BT_nDisable NC -> use a non-wireless CM5.", 384.81, 332.49], ["J4 = Hirose FH12-22S-0.5SH, 22-way 0.5 mm FPC; pinout = CM5IO", 208.28, 379.7], ["CAM/DISP0 (Pi 5 camera cable). MIPI0 D0..D3 + clock, SDA0/SCL0", 208.28, 381.74], ["(1.8k pull-ups inside CM5), CAM_GPIO0 = camera power enable,", 208.28, 383.79], ["CAM_GPIO1 spare, CM5_3.3V on pin 22. D-PHY pairs 100R diff, 0.15 mm.", 208.28, 385.83], ["ESD prot", 68.58, 215.01], ["Power", 185.42, 199.14], ["USB-C Receptacle", 108.71, 171.58], ["CSI camera (MIPI0)", 208.28, 305.19], ["AGND", 111.71, 102.23], ["J1", 109.22, 34.92], ["PC104_H1_H2", 109.22, 37.47], ["THM0", 126.24, 107.31], [